# Rendered media. Big, binary, and reproducible from the scripts in this repo
# (gameshots.py -> promo/shot-*.mp4, harvest_stills.py -> store/stills/).
# Git keeps every version of a binary forever, so ~140 MB of MP4s would bloat
# the clone permanently for something a re-render regenerates.
# `promo/` is ignored for the MEDIA. QUEUE.md and POSTED.md live there too and
# are hand-kept text that no script regenerates - two routines read them, so
# losing them loses the marketing state. Git will not descend into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so the pattern has to be `promo/*` for the negations to work.
promo/*
!promo/QUEUE.md
!promo/POSTED.md
!promo/*_draft.md
# ...and the GENERATORS, added 2026-09-10. The rationale at the top of this file
# is that promo media is "reproducible from the scripts in this repo" - but the
# scripts were ignored too, so it was not true of anything under promo/: a fresh
# clone could not rebuild the resample card or the density card. The .py/.html
# under here is hand-written source that no script regenerates, same category as
# QUEUE.md above. The _facts.json files are kept because they are what the
# captions are substituted from, and a card whose numbers cannot be re-derived
# is exactly the thing these generators exist to prevent. Media stays ignored.
!promo/*/
promo/*/*
!promo/*/*.py
!promo/*/*.html
!promo/*/*.json
store/stills/
gallery/
shots/panels/
# Raw Blender viewport screenshots, added 2026-09-10 by pixelkiln-backup.
# density_shot.py writes shots/density/*.png with bpy.ops.screen.screenshot
# and re-running it reproduces them byte-identically, so they are build
# artifacts in the same category as shots/panels/ above - 7.4 MB of them,
# in a PUBLIC repo. shots/density/facts.json is NOT ignored: make_density.py
# reads it as its input, so it is the record the card's numbers come from.
shots/density/*.png
shots/workspace.png
gif/frames/

# build output
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.coverage

# run logs
e2e.log
*.log

# per-version gate output
versions.log
gui_versions.log
first_run.log
gif/palette.png
_posters/
MARKETING.html
_posters/
MARKETING.html
gif/_assets.json

# Render sweeps for the store background: 4-6 MB PNGs, one keeper each.
store/theme/_bg_src/

# Local backups of settings files, made by hand before an edit: machine safety
# net, never repo history.
*.bak-*

# Scratch verification crops, added 2026-09-11 by pixelkiln-backup. A doer that
# checks its own render writes throwaway views next to it - _crop_head.png,
# _chip_zoom.png, _after_full_view.png. They are the same category as
# shots/density/*.png above: reproducible from the generator and never referenced
# by anything that ships. The funnel's first drop left 636 KB of them and this
# repo has never tracked one, so the pattern is written down rather than
# re-applied by hand every night. Deliverables and published art do NOT start
# with an underscore.
_*.png

# Raw T-008 reproduction frames, added 2026-09-16 by pixelkiln-backup.
# repro_t008.py drives a real GUI Blender and screenshots the whole window;
# shots/t008/ came out at 15 MB across 37 files, of which 15 are ~930 KB
# full-window frames (f0-f3, sidebar, settle/shot_*, and the 4.2.23 rerun).
# They are reproducible by re-running the script, exactly like shots/density/
# *.png and shots/panels/ above, and this repo is PUBLIC.
# The CROPS ARE KEPT and that is deliberate -- ~1.3 MB of region-only captures
# that promo/POSTED.md names as the v0.2.1 before/after library, and a crop is
# what the reproduction actually proves: the panel is the evidence, the window
# around it is not.
shots/t008/f?_*.png
shots/t008/*/f?_*.png
shots/t008/sidebar*.png
shots/t008/settle/shot_*.png

# Browser profiles, lock files and node_modules, added 2026-09-21 by
# pixelkiln-backup. None of the three has ever appeared in this repo, which is
# why the gap went unnoticed: the parent repo ignores all three and this one
# ignored none. A persistent Playwright profile carries a LIVE logged-in
# session, and this repo is PUBLIC, so the one night a script is run with
# --profile from this directory is the night the store's credentials reach a
# public remote. The pattern is cheaper than the discipline of never doing it.
profile/
profile-*/
*.lock
node_modules/
